# CVE-2024-36117 (GHSA-82j3-hf72-7x93, CWE-22): the javadoc raw-resource
# route of Reposilite served any file the process can read. The route
#
#   GET /javadoc/{repository}/<gav>/raw/<resource>
#
# takes the client-controlled `<resource>` path parameter, wraps it in
# reposilite's Location type and serves
# `Files.newInputStream(javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource.toString()))`.
# The wrap does not make the value a safe path: `Location.of` at the
# vulnerable revision only rewrote `\` to `/` and collapsed repeated
# slashes, so `..` segments survive construction, and the serving code
# reads the raw form (`resource.toString()`) rather than the validating
# accessor (`resource.toPath()`, which rejects `..` and `:` outright).
# Resolving `../../../../../../reposilite.db` against the unpack directory
# then reads the sqlite database with password hashes and token data --
# the advisory's own reproduction.
#
# Fix e172ae4b539c822d0d6e04cf090713c7202a79d6 ("Make Location a bit
# safer to use out-of-the-box by immediately sanitazing invalid symbols")
# collapses every run of two or more dots to a single one and strips
# drive-letter colons inside `Location.of` itself, so the raw `toString()`
# form cannot name an ancestor. Row verified: the uncollapsed
# `Location.of` and the `resource.toString()` resolve are present at
# e172ae4b^, the collapse is present at e172ae4b. The advisory's
# suggested remediation (`resource.toPath()` instead of `toString()`)
# names the same asymmetry from the other side: the type has a
# validating accessor; the serving path did not use it.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap. Bindings ship so the Kotlin taint shape is
# reachable at all: Javalin's documented request-parameter accessors
# (`Context.pathParamMap` / `pathParam` / `queryParam`, httpInput400-402)
# and java.nio.file.Files' access operations (filePathAccess403-412), both
# in vyql/bindings/kotlin/m304d1620.vyql -- Kotlin had no source for any
# Javalin parameter read and no sink for any Files call, so VYQL-PATH-001
# could not report this class of route in Kotlin however directly the
# value flowed.
#
# Three findings of the diagnosis, all measured on minimal pairs below:
#
# 1. The Kotlin frontend severed an expression-body function's value from
#    its return. `ktConv.block` (kotlin.go) lowered `fun f() = expr` to a
#    bare ExprStmt, which never reached the `analysis.function.return`
#    node callers read; and an `indexing_expression` body had no `stmt`
#    case at all, so `fun parameter(name: String): String? =
#    ctx.pathParamMap()[name]` -- the exact spelling of Reposilite's
#    ContextDsl.parameter -- lowered to an empty function. The same body
#    written with a block and an explicit return reached the sink. This
#    is the nearest dead-end on the real path; the change (route a
#    function-body expression through nir.Return) ships alongside this
#    spec and the fourth test holds the minimal pair.
#
# 2. The real route's chain is still severed further along, so the first
#    two tests stay quiet and pin those gaps: a bare call to a method
#    inherited from a base class does not resolve (`resolveCallee`'s
#    curClass branch, lowering.go, looks only in the enclosing class and
#    never falls back to the base-class walk used for typed receivers),
#    which is how `requireParameter("resource")` reads inside a route
#    class extending the DSL; an if-expression body's value is still
#    dropped (its value form keeps only each branch's last statement, so
#    routing it through a return is not a safe one-line change); and a
#    value stored through a data-class constructor is not read back from
#    the field the way `with (request) { resource }` reads it.
#
# 3. Even with every hop visible, the change is not discriminable at the
#    dataflow layer. The remediation is a private string sanitizer -- a
#    chained `.replace(Regex("\\.{2,}"), ".")` -- and no layer recognizes
#    a user-defined replace as a traversal neutralizer (every
#    core.PathCanonicalization binding names a canonicalization API such
#    as normalize/canonicalPath/toRealPath). Measured with both bodies
#    spelled so the engine tracks them (block bodies, named receivers):
#    the vulnerable chain and the patched chain BOTH propagate taint to
#    the sink, so the patched revision would report identically. The
#    missing capability is sanitizer modeling for user-defined string
#    transforms, recorded in ENGINE-GAPS.md; keying instead on this
#    fix's own regex spelling would be a repro-shaped patch.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1669: the javadoc raw route resolves the request's resource against the unpack directory and opens it"
  lang kotlin
  file reposilite-backend/src/main/kotlin/com/reposilite/javadocs/JavadocFacade.kt
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.nio.file.Files
  import java.nio.file.Path

  class Context(val pathParamMap: Map<String, String>, val uri: String) {
      fun queryParam(name: String): String? = null
  }

  open class ContextDsl<out R : Any>(private val ctx: Context) {
      fun requireParameter(name: String): String = parameter(name)!!
      fun parameter(name: String): String? = ctx.pathParamMap()[name]
  }

  class Location private constructor(private val uri: String) {
      companion object {
          private val multipleSlashes = Regex("/+")
          fun of(uri: String): Location =
              uri.replace("\\", "/")
                  .replace(multipleSlashes, "/")
                  .let { Location(it) }
      }
      fun toPath(): Path? {
          if (uri.contains("..") || uri.contains(":") || uri.contains("\\")) {
              return null
          }
          return Path.of(uri).normalize()
      }
      override fun toString(): String = uri
  }

  fun String?.toLocation(): Location =
      if (this != null) Location.of(this) else Location.of("")

  class JavadocRawRequest(val repository: String, val gav: Location, val resource: Location)

  class Container(val javadocUnpackPath: Path)

  class JavadocRoutes(val ctx: Context, val container: Container) : ContextDsl<Any>(ctx) {
      fun findRawJavadocResource(): ByteArray {
          val request = JavadocRawRequest("releases", Location.of("javadoc/1.0.0"), requireParameter("resource").toLocation())
          return with (request) {
              Files.exists(container.javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource.toString()))
              Files.newInputStream(container.javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource.toString())).readBytes()
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1669: the same route with Location.of collapsing directory operators at construction"
  lang kotlin
  file reposilite-backend/src/main/kotlin/com/reposilite/javadocs/JavadocFacade.kt
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.nio.file.Files
  import java.nio.file.Path

  class Context(val pathParamMap: Map<String, String>, val uri: String) {
      fun queryParam(name: String): String? = null
  }

  open class ContextDsl<out R : Any>(private val ctx: Context) {
      fun requireParameter(name: String): String = parameter(name)!!
      fun parameter(name: String): String? = ctx.pathParamMap()[name]
  }

  class Location private constructor(private val uri: String) {
      companion object {
          private val multipleSlashes = Regex("/+")
          private val multipleDirectoryOperators = Regex("\\.{2,}")
          fun of(uri: String): Location =
              uri.replaceBefore(":", "")
                  .replace(":", "")
                  .replace(multipleDirectoryOperators, ".")
                  .replace("\\", "/")
                  .replace(multipleSlashes, "/")
                  .let { Location(it) }
      }
      fun toPath(): Path? {
          if (uri.contains(":") || uri.contains("\\") || uri.contains(multipleDirectoryOperators)) {
              return null
          }
          return Path.of(uri).normalize()
      }
      override fun toString(): String = uri
  }

  fun String?.toLocation(): Location =
      if (this != null) Location.of(this) else Location.of("")

  class JavadocRawRequest(val repository: String, val gav: Location, val resource: Location)

  class Container(val javadocUnpackPath: Path)

  class JavadocRoutes(val ctx: Context, val container: Container) : ContextDsl<Any>(ctx) {
      fun findRawJavadocResource(): ByteArray {
          val request = JavadocRawRequest("releases", Location.of("javadoc/1.0.0"), requireParameter("resource").toLocation())
          return with (request) {
              Files.exists(container.javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource.toString()))
              Files.newInputStream(container.javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource.toString())).readBytes()
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1669: the parameter read reaches the file open when every function returns its value in a block body"
  lang kotlin
  file reposilite-backend/src/main/kotlin/com/reposilite/javadocs/JavadocFacade.kt
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  import java.nio.file.Files
  import java.nio.file.Path

  class Context {
      fun pathParamMap(): Map<String, String> = mapOf()
  }

  class ContextDsl(private val ctx: Context) {
      fun requireParameter(name: String): String {
          val value = parameter(name)
          return value!!
      }
      fun parameter(name: String): String? {
          val map = ctx.pathParamMap()
          return map[name]
      }
  }

  class Container(val javadocUnpackPath: Path)

  class JavadocRoutes(private val dsl: ContextDsl, private val container: Container) {
      fun findRawJavadocResource(): ByteArray {
          val resource = dsl.requireParameter("resource")
          return Files.newInputStream(container.javadocUnpackPath.resolve(resource)).readBytes()
      }
  }
  ```

